#. translators: %d: number of further pages
#: src/Support/ReportBuilder.php:187
#, php-format
msgid "…and %d more pages"
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/ReportBuilder.php:194
msgid "Pages that could not be checked"
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/ReportBuilder.php:210
msgid "Manual checks to do next"
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/ReportBuilder.php:212
msgid "Use the site with only a keyboard (Tab, Shift+Tab, Enter, Space, Esc). Can you reach and use every link, menu, form and pop-up, and always see where focus is?"
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/ReportBuilder.php:213
msgid "Zoom the browser to 200% and 400%. Does everything still fit and work without scrolling sideways?"
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/ReportBuilder.php:214
msgid "Try a screen reader (VoiceOver on Mac/iPhone, NVDA on Windows, TalkBack on Android) on your key pages and forms."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/ReportBuilder.php:215
msgid "Check that alt text is meaningful, videos have accurate captions, and form errors are explained in text."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/ReportBuilder.php:216
msgid "Publish an accessibility statement with a way for visitors to report problems (required for public sector sites and expected under the European Accessibility Act)."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/ReportBuilder.php:218
msgid "Need a full manual audit, fixes or an accessibility statement? iWorks can help: https://www.iworks.ie"
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:37
msgid "Open the technical guidance link below for the exact requirement. If the element comes from a plugin or theme, ask its developer to fix it."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:48
msgid "In the block editor select the image and fill in \"Alternative text\" in the block settings, or edit the image in Media Library. Describe what the image shows or does. If it is purely decorative, leave the alt text empty on purpose (in code: alt=\"\")."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:49
msgid "Screen readers announce this control with no name, so people who cannot see it do not know what it does."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:53
msgid "Images are missing alternative text"
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:54
msgid "Blind and low-vision visitors use screen readers that read alt text aloud. Without it they hear the file name or nothing at all."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:58
msgid "Image buttons have no text alternative"
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:60
msgid "Add an alt attribute to the image button that says what it does, for example alt=\"Search\". This usually lives in a theme or plugin template."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:63
msgid "Elements shown as images have no text alternative"
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:64
msgid "The element is marked as an image (role=\"img\") but has no text describing it, so screen reader users miss its meaning."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:65
msgid "Add an aria-label describing the image, or aria-hidden=\"true\" if it is decorative. Icon fonts and CSS background images often cause this."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:68
msgid "SVG images have no text alternative"
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:69
msgid "Screen readers cannot describe an SVG graphic that has no title or label."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:70
msgid "Add a <title> inside the SVG or an aria-label on it. If the SVG is decorative (for example an icon next to text), add aria-hidden=\"true\" instead."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:73
msgid "Image map areas have no text alternative"
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:74
msgid "Each clickable area of an image map is a link. Without alt text, screen reader users cannot tell where it goes."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:75
msgid "Give every <area> element an alt attribute naming its destination, or replace the image map with normal links."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:78
msgid "Embedded objects have no text alternative"
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:79
msgid "Content embedded with <object> is invisible to screen readers unless it has a text alternative."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:80
msgid "Add an aria-label or title to the <object>, or provide the same content as text or a link next to it."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:83
msgid "Alt text repeats the text next to the image"
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:84
msgid "Screen reader users hear the same words twice, which is tiring and confusing."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:85
msgid "Change the image alt text so it adds information, or leave it empty if the caption or link text already says everything."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:88
msgid "Text does not have enough colour contrast"
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:89
msgid "Low-contrast text is hard or impossible to read for people with low vision or colour blindness, and for everyone on a phone in sunlight. WCAG AA needs 4.5:1 for normal text and 3:1 for large text."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:90
msgid "Make the text darker or the background lighter (or the other way round). In the block editor use the block's Color settings, which warn about low contrast. For theme-wide colours, change them in Appearance → Editor → Styles or the Customizer."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:93
msgid "Links have no text"
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:94
msgid "A link with no readable text is announced as just \"link\", so keyboard and screen reader users cannot tell where it goes. This often happens with icon-only social links or linked images with no alt text."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:95
msgid "Add visible link text, or alt text on the linked image, or an aria-label on the link (for example aria-label=\"iWorks on LinkedIn\"). For Social Icons blocks, fill in each icon's label."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:98
msgid "Links inside text can only be spotted by colour"
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:99
msgid "People who cannot tell colours apart will not notice a link that differs from the surrounding text only by colour."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:100
msgid "Underline links inside paragraphs (most themes allow this in Styles → Elements → Links), or make sure the link colour has 3:1 contrast with the text and changes on hover and focus."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:103
msgid "Buttons have no accessible name"
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:105
msgid "Give the button visible text, or an aria-label describing what it does (for example aria-label=\"Open menu\"). Icon-only buttons in headers, sliders and pop-ups are the usual culprits."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:108
msgid "Input buttons have no text"
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:110
msgid "Add a value attribute (the button text) to the <input type=\"submit|button|reset\">, or an aria-label."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:113
msgid "Form fields have no label"
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:114
msgid "Without a label, screen reader users do not know what to type into the field. Placeholder text is not a label: it disappears once typing starts."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:115
msgid "In your form plugin, make sure every field has a label (you can visually hide it if the design needs that, but do not delete it). In code, connect a <label for=\"…\"> to the field's id."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:118
msgid "Drop-down lists have no label"
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:119
msgid "Screen reader users hear \"combo box\" with no idea what they are choosing."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:120
msgid "Add a label to the drop-down in your form plugin or template, or an aria-label if a visible label is not possible."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:123
msgid "Form fields have more than one label"
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:124
msgid "Assistive technology may read only one of the labels, or read them in a confusing order."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:125
msgid "Keep one <label> per field. Put extra hints in a description linked with aria-describedby."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:128
msgid "Form autocomplete values are invalid"
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:129
msgid "Correct autocomplete values let browsers fill in name, email and address fields, which helps people with motor and memory difficulties."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:130
msgid "Use a standard value such as autocomplete=\"email\", \"name\" or \"postal-code\". Many form plugins have an autocomplete setting per field."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:133
msgid "The page has no title"
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:134
msgid "The page title is the first thing a screen reader announces and the label on the browser tab. Without it people cannot tell pages apart."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:135
msgid "Make sure the theme supports \"title-tag\" (add_theme_support( 'title-tag' )) or outputs a <title>. SEO plugins also set it."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:138
msgid "The page language is not set"
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:139
msgid "Screen readers use the page language to choose the right voice and pronunciation. Without it, English text may be read with the wrong accent, or the other way round."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:140
msgid "The theme's header should output <html <?php language_attributes(); ?>>. Check Settings → General → Site Language too."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:143
msgid "The page language code is not valid"
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:144
msgid "An unrecognised language code is as bad as none: screen readers fall back to a default voice."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:145
msgid "Use a valid code such as en, en-IE or ga. Check Settings → General → Site Language and any multilingual plugin settings."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:148
msgid "The page has two different language settings"
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:149
msgid "When lang and xml:lang disagree, assistive technology may pick the wrong language."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:150
msgid "Remove xml:lang from the <html> element, or make it match lang."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:153
msgid "A language code inside the page is not valid"
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:154
msgid "Sections in another language should be marked so they are pronounced correctly. An invalid code breaks this."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:155
msgid "Correct the lang attribute on the element shown, for example lang=\"ga\" for Irish or lang=\"fr\" for French."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:158
msgid "Heading levels skip a step"
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:159
msgid "Screen reader users jump between headings to scan a page, like a table of contents. Skipping levels (H2 straight to H4) makes the structure confusing."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:160
msgid "Choose heading levels by structure, not by size: H2 for sections, H3 inside them. Change the look with the block's typography settings instead of picking a smaller heading level."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:163
msgid "Headings are empty"
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:164
msgid "Screen readers announce an empty heading, which is confusing and wastes time."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:165
msgid "Delete empty Heading blocks, or add text. Some page builders leave empty headings behind when a widget is hidden."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:168
msgid "The page has no main heading (H1)"
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:169
msgid "The H1 tells visitors what the page is about. Screen reader users often jump to it first."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:170
msgid "Make sure the page title is shown as an H1 (most themes do this), or add one Heading block set to H1 at the top."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:173
msgid "The page has no main content area"
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:174
msgid "A <main> landmark lets keyboard and screen reader users skip straight past the header and menu to the content."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:175
msgid "The theme should wrap the content in <main>. In block themes, set the content Group block's HTML element to <main> under Advanced."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:178
msgid "Some content is outside any page region"
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:179
msgid "Screen reader users navigate by regions (header, navigation, main, footer). Content outside them is easy to miss."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:180
msgid "Make sure everything sits inside <header>, <nav>, <main>, <aside> or <footer>. Cookie banners and chat widgets often cause this; ask their developer, or use the HTML element setting on Group blocks."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:183
msgid "There is no way to skip to the main content"
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:184
msgid "Keyboard users must tab through the whole menu on every page unless there is a skip link or landmarks."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:185
msgid "Add a \"Skip to content\" link as the first focusable element and a <main> landmark. Most modern themes include both; older themes may not."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:188
msgid "The skip link points nowhere"
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:189
msgid "A \"Skip to content\" link whose target does not exist leaves keyboard users stuck at the top."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:190
msgid "Make the skip link's href (for example #content) match the id of the main content element."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:193
msgid "Lists are built incorrectly"
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:194
msgid "Screen readers announce how many items a list has. Lists with other elements directly inside them break this."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:195
msgid "<ul> and <ol> may only contain <li> items (and script/template tags). Usually a theme or plugin template needs fixing."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:198
msgid "List items are outside a list"
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:199
msgid "A list item with no list around it is not announced as part of a list."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:200
msgid "Wrap <li> elements in a <ul> or <ol>."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:203
msgid "Definition lists are built incorrectly"
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:204
msgid "Screen readers rely on correct structure to pair terms with their definitions."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:205
msgid "<dl> may only contain <dt> and <dd> groups (optionally wrapped in <div>)."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:208
msgid "Definition terms are outside a definition list"
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:209
msgid "Terms and definitions outside a <dl> lose their relationship."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:210
msgid "Wrap <dt> and <dd> elements in a <dl>."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:213
msgid "IDs used by labels are duplicated"
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:214
msgid "When two elements share an id that a label or ARIA attribute points to, assistive technology may announce the wrong one."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:215
msgid "Make every id unique on the page. Repeated widgets or forms shown twice (for example in a header and a footer) are the usual cause."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:218
msgid "Embedded frames have no title"
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:219
msgid "Screen reader users hear \"frame\" with no idea whether it is a video, a map or a form."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:220
msgid "Add a title attribute to the <iframe>, for example title=\"Map of our office\". Many embed blocks and plugins have a title setting."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:223
msgid "Embedded frames share the same title"
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:224
msgid "Identical titles make it impossible to tell embedded frames apart."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:225
msgid "Give each <iframe> a title that describes its own content."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:228
msgid "Frames with interactive content cannot be reached by keyboard"
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:229
msgid "Keyboard users cannot reach links or buttons inside the frame."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:230
msgid "Remove tabindex=\"-1\" from the <iframe> when it contains links, buttons or form fields."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:233
msgid "Zooming is disabled"
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:234
msgid "People with low vision pinch to zoom on phones. Blocking zoom makes the site unreadable for them."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:235
msgid "Remove user-scalable=no and any maximum-scale below 2 from the viewport meta tag, usually in the theme's header.php or a plugin setting."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:238
msgid "The page refreshes or redirects on a timer"
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:239
msgid "An automatic refresh can move people away before they finish reading, and screen readers start again from the top."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:240
msgid "Remove the meta refresh tag. Use a proper server redirect instead (for example with a redirection plugin)."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:243
msgid "Clickable targets are too small or too close together"
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:244
msgid "Small targets are hard to tap for people with tremors, large fingers or on a moving bus. WCAG 2.2 asks for at least 24 by 24 pixels or enough space around them."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:245
msgid "Increase padding on small links and buttons (pagination, social icons, carousel dots), or add space between them."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:248
msgid "Scrollable areas cannot be scrolled with the keyboard"
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:249
msgid "If a box scrolls but cannot receive keyboard focus, keyboard users cannot read what is hidden inside it."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:250
msgid "Add tabindex=\"0\" and an accessible name (aria-label) to the scrolling element, or make sure it contains a focusable element."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:253
msgid "Interactive controls are nested inside each other"
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:254
msgid "A button inside a link (or similar) confuses screen readers and keyboard focus: one of them is often unreachable."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:255
msgid "Restructure so links and buttons sit side by side, not inside each other. Card designs in page builders are a common cause."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:258
msgid "Hidden elements can still receive keyboard focus"
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:259
msgid "Keyboard users land on links or buttons that screen readers say do not exist, which is very disorienting."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:260
msgid "Either remove aria-hidden=\"true\", or make the focusable elements inside it unfocusable (tabindex=\"-1\") or hidden with display:none. Off-canvas menus and sliders often cause this."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:263
msgid "The whole page is hidden from screen readers"
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:264
msgid "aria-hidden on <body> hides the entire site from assistive technology."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:265
msgid "Remove aria-hidden=\"true\" from the <body> element. A pop-up or modal plugin usually adds it."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:268
msgid "ARIA attributes are used on the wrong elements"
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:269
msgid "ARIA attributes that do not belong to an element's role are ignored or misread by assistive technology."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:270
msgid "Remove the attribute or change the element's role. This is almost always in theme or plugin code; report it to the developer."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:273
msgid "ARIA roles are missing required attributes"
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:274
msgid "Some roles need extra information (for example a checkbox needs aria-checked) or screen readers cannot report their state."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:275
msgid "Add the missing attribute named in the details, or use a native HTML element (<button>, <input type=\"checkbox\">) which provides it automatically."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:278
msgid "ARIA widgets are missing required child elements"
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:279
msgid "Roles like list, menu or tablist must contain the right child roles or screen readers cannot navigate them."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:280
msgid "Add the required child roles (for example role=\"tab\" inside role=\"tablist\"), or remove the parent role."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:283
msgid "ARIA elements are missing their required parent"
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:284
msgid "Roles like tab or menuitem only make sense inside their container role."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:285
msgid "Wrap the elements in the required parent role, or remove their role attribute."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:288
msgid "ARIA attributes are misspelled or do not exist"
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:289
msgid "Unknown ARIA attributes are ignored, so the information they were meant to give is lost."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:290
msgid "Correct the attribute name (for example aria-labelledby, not aria-labeledby)."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:293
msgid "ARIA attributes have invalid values"
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:294
msgid "An invalid value (for example aria-expanded=\"yes\" or a reference to an id that does not exist) is ignored or misreported."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:295
msgid "Use a valid value: true/false for states, and ids that exist on the page for references."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:298
msgid "Elements use ARIA roles that do not exist"
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:299
msgid "An invalid role is ignored, so the element is announced incorrectly."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:300
msgid "Correct or remove the role attribute."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:303
msgid "ARIA buttons, links or menu items have no name"
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:305
msgid "Add text inside the element or an aria-label."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:308
msgid "ARIA input fields have no name"
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:309
msgid "Screen reader users do not know what to enter in the field."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:310
msgid "Add an aria-label or aria-labelledby pointing to visible label text."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:313
msgid "ARIA toggles have no name"
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:314
msgid "Screen reader users hear \"switch\" or \"checkbox\" without knowing what it controls."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:315
msgid "Add visible text or an aria-label to the toggle."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:318
msgid "ARIA labels are used where they are not allowed"
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:319
msgid "Some elements (like a plain <div> or <span>) cannot be named with aria-label, so the label is never announced."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:320
msgid "Move the label onto an element that supports it, give the element a suitable role, or use visible text instead."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:323
msgid "Elements force a custom keyboard order"
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:324
msgid "A tabindex above 0 makes focus jump around the page in an unexpected order."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:325
msgid "Remove positive tabindex values (use 0 or -1 only) and order the HTML the way it should be read."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:328
msgid "Table cells point to headers that do not exist"
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:329
msgid "Screen readers announce the column and row headers for each cell. Broken references remove that context."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:330
msgid "Make the headers attribute point to the ids of header cells in the same table, or remove it and use <th scope>."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:333
msgid "Table headers have no data cells"
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:334
msgid "A header that describes nothing suggests the table is used for layout or built incorrectly."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:335
msgid "Remove empty header cells, or use the Table block with a header section only when the table holds data."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:338
msgid "Table headers are empty"
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:339
msgid "Screen readers announce header text for every cell. An empty header gives no context."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:340
msgid "Add text to each header cell, or use a normal <td> for empty corner cells."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:343
msgid "Videos have no captions"
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:344
msgid "Deaf and hard-of-hearing visitors, and anyone watching with the sound off, miss what is said."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:345
msgid "Add a captions track: in the Video block use \"Text tracks\" to upload a .vtt file. For YouTube and Vimeo, add captions on those platforms."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:348
msgid "Audio plays automatically"
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:349
msgid "Sound that starts on its own drowns out screen readers and is distressing for many people."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:350
msgid "Turn off autoplay on audio and video, or make it muted and provide a pause control."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:353
msgid "Text blinks"
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:354
msgid "Blinking content is distracting and can be hard to read for people with attention or vision difficulties."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:355
msgid "Remove the <blink> element."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:358
msgid "Text scrolls automatically"
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:359
msgid "Moving text is hard to read and cannot be paused by everyone."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:360
msgid "Remove the <marquee> element, or replace it with static text."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:363
msgid "Inline styles stop people adjusting text spacing"
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:364
msgid "People with dyslexia or low vision often increase line and letter spacing with a browser tool. !important inline styles block that."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:365
msgid "Remove !important from inline line-height, letter-spacing and word-spacing styles."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:368
msgid "The accessible name does not match the visible text"
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:369
msgid "Voice control users say the words they can see. If the hidden label is different, the command does not work."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:370
msgid "Make the aria-label start with (or contain) the visible text of the control."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:373
msgid "Form fields are labelled only with a tooltip"
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:374
msgid "Title tooltips are not shown on touch screens or to keyboard users, and not reliably read by screen readers."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:375
msgid "Add a proper visible <label> for the field."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:378
msgid "Page regions of the same type have the same name"
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:379
msgid "Two navigation menus both announced as \"navigation\" are impossible to tell apart."
msgstr ""

#: src/Support/RuleGuide.php:380
